meta {
  name: shell hooks read-out
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/settings/hooks
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  ~session: {{sessionId}}
}

docs {
  The configured shell hooks READ OUT: per scope and folded, each with the matcher and the timeout it will ACTUALLY run under, raw and resolved side by side. hooks is a whole-block field — the highest layer that sets it replaces every layer below; the read-out exists to carry that fact.
  
  Fence: host — Loopback fence: the TCP peer must be loopback AND the Host header must be localhost/127.0.0.1/::1. A REST client passes automatically when it targets http://localhost:<port>. A LAN IP or rebound DNS name in the URL answers a blank 404.
  
  Writes state: no
}
